{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 400}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 101, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 3 absent, edge 5 is a key route to the output, and removing it can disconnect the cell (about -60 to -70 points in several runs)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing avg_pool on the direct input-to-output edge with a conv gave large gains (+12 to +15 points) in several runs, more than other replacements."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 3 is absent, removing edge 4 often cuts the output off, giving drops of 50 to 77 points."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a parameter-free pool on the input edge for a 3x3 conv gave consistent gains (+5 to +10 points in several runs)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with pooling on edge 2 hurt consistently across datasets, by up to -9 to -15 points."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv to an empty edge 5 restored an output path and gave large gains (+15 to +20 points in several runs)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with an identity on edge 4 lost capacity and caused large drops of -4 to -20 points."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a 3x3 conv on edge 1 removes useful feature extraction and hurt on all three datasets, especially ImageNet16-120."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3,